<!--
Phase 1: The Form Foundation and Intercept 
Requirements
Build the form interface and take complete control of the form submission process using JavaScript:

Create an HTML page (index.html) containing a <form id="feedback-form"> with:
A text input for the reviewer’s name (id="reviewer-name").
A number input (or dropdown <select>) for the star rating from 1 to 5 (id="rating").
A <textarea> for detailed comments (id="comments").
A submit button (<button type="submit">Submit Feedback</button>).
A dedicated container (such as a <div id="error-box"></div>) to hold validation messages.
Attach a submit event listener to the form.
Prevent the default browser form submission action so the page does not refresh or navigate away when submitted.
In the console, log the entered values of all three inputs to verify that you can extract their current values. 
-->

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Sunnydale Solutions - Customer Feedback</title>
</head>

<body>

    <form id="feedback-form" novalidate>

        <label for="reviewer-name">Your Name:</label>
        <input id="reviewer-name">

        <label for="rating">Star Rating:</label>
        <input type="number" id="rating" min="1" max="5">
        
        <label for="comments">Comments:</label>
        <textarea id="comments"></textarea>

        <button type="submit">Submit Feedback</button>

        <div id="error-box"></div>
    
    </form>

<script src="script.js"></script>

</body>

</html>